  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$y^2=16 x ; a=4 \\quad$ focus $S \\equiv(4,0)$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Z36FNxKiDIX337k0mKii2aIOOLDBEUB05LWYj157Zzw.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & 2 \\mathrm{at}_1=-4 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 2(4) \\mathrm{t}_1=-4 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}_1=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ & \\because \\mathrm{t}_1 \\mathrm{t}_2=-1\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}_2=2 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{Q}\\left(\\mathrm{at}_2^2, 2 \\mathrm{at}_2\\right)=(16,16)<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>Let, S divides PQ internally in $\\lambda: 1$ ratio<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\therefore \\frac{16 \\lambda-4}{\\lambda+1}=0 \\\\\n& \\lambda=\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{n}} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{~m}^2+\\mathrm{n}^2=1+16=17<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
